  "id": "process-model-of-emotion-regulation",
  "term": "process model of emotion regulation",
  "definition": "The process model of emotion regulation is a framework for understanding how people manage emotions using different strategies. In this packet, it is described through reappraisal, which changes one’s psychological state in a situation, and expressive suppression, which modifies emotional expression after an emotion has already begun.",
